        "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 7 at 9:49PM PST until November 10 at 12:00PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Minor to locally moderate coastal flooding expected.\nAdditionally, dangerous rip currents and surf of 3 to 6 feet\nexpected along west-facing beaches.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...Through noon PST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Highest tides will occur in the late\nmorning each day, peaking at 7.4-7.6 feet Sunday and Monday,\nwhich is 1.3 to 1.6 feet above astronomical tide predictions.\nSurf will increase to 4-7 feet Monday, which may prolong some\nof the coastal impacts.",
        "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
        "response": "Monitor",
        "note": null,
